+T831 (2026-08-24): on failure the TWO QUESTIONS are named apart.  The nonce
+is proof-of-READING (did the worker open its instructions); the deliverables
+are proof-of-WORK (did the work happen).  A worker whose declared
+deliverables all exist and parse but that never echoed the token reports
+PROTOCOL FAILURE — a proof-of-reading breach, never to be confused with a
+worker that read its brief and produced nothing (the T818 orphan: a finished
+task read as a failure for two hours because only the nonce arm spoke).
+The graded contract does not move: exit stays 2, verified stays fail,
+fail_check stays nonce/deliverables (model-profiles RECOVERABLE_FAIL grades
+both recoverable — correct, a protocol breach is re-runnable); only the
+human-readable verdict names WHICH question broke.  The same edit closes
+T793's recorded defect: a success-verdict row with NO deliverables declared
+is UNVERIFIABLE, never PASS.
+
